CONTEXT CostGate IN ENGLISH

-- Model for the cost-gate regression (Ampersand issue #1692).
--
-- It is deliberately small and carries one conjunct of each kind the gate must
-- treat differently:
--   guestName  a UNI relation stored on the Booking key column — the layout
--              enforces univalence, so its UNI conjunct is the structural case
--   note       a second UNI relation, so the spec can assert that skipping one
--              conjunct leaves its neighbours untouched
--   follows    a plain relation carrying an ordinary rule — no table layout
--              enforces it, which makes it the counterexample of scenario 3
--
-- The interface is rooted in SESSION, the shape the framework's resource API
-- navigates; it also gives Booking the Object representation and hence a
-- primary key, without which no conjunct qualifies as structural.

CONCEPT Booking "A booking"
REPRESENT Name TYPE ALPHANUMERIC

RELATION guestName[Booking*Name] [UNI]
MEANING "The name of the guest for a booking."
RELATION note[Booking*Name] [UNI]
MEANING "A free-text note on a booking."
RELATION follows[Booking*Booking]
MEANING "A booking that follows another one."

RULE NoSelfFollow LABEL "A booking does not follow itself":
  follows |- -I[Booking]
MEANING "A booking cannot follow itself."
VIOLATION (TXT "Booking ", SRC I, TXT " follows itself.")

RELATION allBookings[SESSION*Booking]
ROLE ExecEngine MAINTAINS ShowAllBookings
RULE ShowAllBookings: V[SESSION*Booking] |- allBookings
VIOLATION (TXT "{EX} InsPair;allBookings;SESSION;", SRC I, TXT ";Booking;", TGT I)

INTERFACE Bookings : "_SESSION"[SESSION] cRud BOX<TABLE>
  [ "Bookings" : allBookings cRud BOX<FORM>
      [ "Guest name" : guestName cRUd
      , "Note" : note cRUd
      , "Follows" : follows cRUd
      ]
  ]

POPULATION Booking CONTAINS [ "booking1", "booking2" ]

ENDCONTEXT
